{"ts": "2026-09-23T17:51:42", "conversation_id": "20260923T174924-8f513591", "role": "user", "kind": "prompt", "content": "You are fixing a GitHub issue. Follow the existing code style,\nnaming conventions, and architecture visible in the files below. Do not\nintroduce new dependencies or restructure unrelated code.\n\nISSUE TITLE: SMS connector: document provider abstraction boundary\nISSUE DESCRIPTION:\nParent: #34\n\n## Problem\nShops may want SMS alerts through different providers. Posnic should define the abstraction before adding provider-specific code.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Document common SMS provider inputs: destination, template/message, sender id, status callback, and cost/error metadata.\n- [ ] Define privacy and opt-in boundaries for customer phone numbers.\n- [ ] Propose a fake SMS provider fixture for tests.\n- [ ] State that no real SMS is sent by default.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Integrating a specific SMS provider.\n- Marketing automation.\n\nISSUE LABELS: documentation, good first issue, help wanted, area: integrations, needs evidence, size: small, community edition, security\nDOMAIN: this issue lives in the docs area -- respect that layer's conventions (e.g. typed API surfaces, framework idioms, model/data contracts) and do not leak concerns across layers.\n\n\nRELEVANT FILES:\n--- frontend/static/script/js/modules/js/sales.js ---\n\ufeffPosnicPro.sales = {\n    /* Array Declaration */\n    extraDiscount: [],\n    addLineTable: [],\n    addSalesLineTable: [],\n    returnSalesLineTable: [],\n    SaleTableLineItems: [],\n    addSalesItemChars: [],\n    EditRecentSaleParams: [],\n    submissionInProgress: false,\n    SaleDenomination: [],\n    tablesList: [],\n    selectedTable: null,\n    selectedPerson: null,\n    currentItemNoteId: null,\n    dineType: 'Dine-in',\n    recentSaleAction: false,\n    recentSaleId: '',\n    editSaleAction: false,\n    editSaleId: '',\n    salesId: '',\n    refundSaleAction: false,\n    refundSaleId: '',\n    